2 CONT '''Merits'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Behmer, before the nobility Daniel Jonæ Gewalius , later Gislenius (Gislenus, Gissel) and finally, from 1638, Behm, b. Oct. 1611 in Gävle, d. Dec. 29, 1669 in Älvkarleby. Parents: mayor John Mickelsson and Anna Danielsdotte
2 CONC r Kröger. Enjoyed school education in Gävle; student in Uppsala 1 Feb. 1626; disp. 18 June 1631 (Disputationum de usu logices secunda, legitimum logicæ in SS theologiâ usum ostendens generatim; pres. L. Stigzelius, resp. Dan. Jonæ
2 CONC  Gewalius) and 29 Apr. 1634 (De habitibus, ut in anima sunt, generatim & communibus nonullis eorum divisionibus; pres. MO Stenius, resp. Dan. Jonæ Gislenus); informant for Axel Oxenstierna's son Erik June 1634–1638; undertook a fo
2 CONC reign trip 1 Aug. 1638–Nov. 1640. Professor of eloquence in Uppsala 16 Nov. 1640; Secretary of the Crown 14 Jan. 1645; District Governor of Långhundra and Tuhundra District 3 Jan. 1646; Assessor in the Svea Court of Appeal 17 Apr.
2 CONC  1649; knighted 15 June 1650; Assessor of the second class 23 Nov. 1654; State Secretary Apr. 1655; also Commissioner in the Reduction Board 1655–62; Councilor of the Court 13 Dec. 1664; member of the Lower Court of Justice with t
2 CONC he task of presiding there in the absence of the Chancellor of the Court 22 Nov. 1666.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1) 26 July 1643 to Brita Schütte, b. 10 Nov. 1623, d. 18 May 1668, daughter of the alderman and merchant in Nyköping Henning Schütte; 2) 24 Apr. 1669 with Magdalena Lindegren, b. 18 June 1646, daughter of the assessor in t
2 CONC he Göta Court of Appeal Nils Lindegren and remarried to the cavalry master Karl Gustav Lood.
