2 CONC reakthrough of the 1570s (1965); its, Pig's Head and Pig's Ball (PHT 1966, 3–4); S Carlsson, Estate society and estate persons 1700–1865 (1947); Carpelan, 3 (1965); Diplomatarium Dalekarlicum, 1–3 o supplement (1842–53); The elect
2 CONC ric trails; H Gillingstam, Svinhuvud och Svinakula (PHT 1966, 1–2); LF Läffler, Some Swedish "talking weapons" (PHT 1903), pp. 77 o 83; BA Nelson, S in Västergötland: some contributions to the genealogy of the family (SoH 1967); J
2 CONC  Raneke, Swedish Medieval Weapons, 1 (1982), p 324, o 3 (1985); SMoK; Supplement to The Introduced Swedish Nobility Genealogies, ed C Szabad (2008); PG Vejde,
2 CONT
