1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Christoffer Olofsson (Stjärna)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Olof Olofsson (Stjärna) and Ingeborg Jönsdotter (Svinhufvud) 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000002514779641&photo_id=6000000194350604029&position=0 Kristoffer Olofsson's maternal grandfather was the miner Jöns Hansson at Höjen, mentioned 1450-1452. What wa
2 CONC s previously known about his (Kristoffer's) daughter Beata was that she was the mother of the mountain man first in Kämparvet and later in Klingsbo Jöns Bengtsson (died 1612/13). The family investigation in this case in Svea Hovrä
2 CONC tt shows that she must have later remarried to the armorer at Halla in Björksta in Västmanland Jon Larsson (beam with three roses)and died around 1543 (Svea Hovrätt, Huvudserie (Liber causarum), SE/RA/ 420422/01/E VI a 2 aa/126 (1
2 CONC 649), image ID: A0068045_00297.]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Bergmästare 1525. /OSN
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kristoffer_Olsson Kristoffer Olsson, Swedish Mountain Bailiff and Mountain Master]
2 CONT
2 CONT Kristoffer Olsson , mountain bailiff and mountain master at Stora Kopparberget probably died, 1531 . Son of Olof Olsson in Hosjö parish in Vika parish ( Stjärna, Kopparbergsätten ) and Ingeborg Jönsdotter (Svinhuvud), married to A
2 CONC nna, "widow in Korsnäs", brother of bishop Otto Svinhufvud and bore the star coat of arms, a six-pointed star (unlike Otto Svinhufvud who carried a combination of the star coat of arms and the boar's head coat of arms in a four-pi
2 CONC ece shield).
2 CONT
2 CONT Kristoffer Olsson is mentioned as mountain bailiff at Stora Kopparberget for the first time in 1502 and some of the following years. In 1521 he is again mountain bailiff, and in 1528 he is mentioned as mountain master.
