1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born to a Swedish family, John Hesselius became one of the leading portrait painters in the Mid-Atlantic colonies. He is noted as one of the earliest teacher of Charles Willson Peale, who later became one of Americ
2 CONC a's best-known colonial artists and whom Hesselius met at Annapolis in the early 1760s.
2 CONT
2 CONT He first studied with his father, Gustavus Hesselius, a painter of portraits and religious subjects, but it is not thought that his father had much influence on his style.
2 CONT
2 CONT Settled in Maryland and painted more than a hundred portraits of Southern and Philadelphia families. He was an early instructor of Charles Willson Peale
2 CONT
2 CONT http://bjws.blogspot.com/2009/03/paintings-john-hesselius_8353.html
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Hesselius
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hesselius (1728–1778) was a portraitist who worked mostly in Virginia and Maryland. He was the son of the Swedish-born portraitist Gustavus Hesselius.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Hesselius?wprov=sfla1
