1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Anders Haroldsson Appelbom=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Anders Andersson Appelbom and Malin Andersdotter
2 CONT * Died abroad before 1687
2 CONT * Appelbom first married on 11 April 1639 to Malin Andersdotter (born 1615), daughter of councilor Anders Andersson and Ingrid Hansdotter Svan in Stockholm . Together they had the children registrar Anders Appelbom and Ingrid Appe
2 CONC lbom (died 1684) who was married to colonel Hieronymus Lindeberg .The son Anders Appelbom was a registrar in the office and is said to have died abroad. As a wife, the latter had married a daughter of Daniel Behmer from his first 
2 CONC marriage. The latter had a son, Harald Appelbom (1669-1730), court assessor and married to Barbara Magdalena Ehrenhielm whose mother was a Gyldenbring , with whom he had several children who died in infancy, a daughter married to 
2 CONC Ehrenhielm, and the son Harald Appelbom (1711-1783) who was chancellor and married the first time to a Gyldenbring, with whom he had two children who died young. Thus the oldest branch of the family started.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Appelbom_nr_325#TAB_4 Noble Family Appelbom no. 325, by Adelsvapen Genealogies]  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TABLE 4'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Anders Appelbom''' (son of Anders Appelbom, table 3 ). Registrar in the Royal Chancellery. Should have then become an officer in Holland and died abroad before 1687. [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000012724059642?album_ty
2 CONC pe=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000218517058821 '''Marriage Record:''' Married on 06-04-1667 in Stockholm to Anna Behmer, daughter of court councilor Daniel Behmer and his 1st wife Brita Schulte.]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Harald Andersson Appelblom,''' born in 1669. Deputy attorney general. Died 1730
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =RSK 7=
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000225661658881&size=large}}  b
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://runeberg.org/strokirk/1/0243.html  	Cultural and personal history notes / First part / 239 (1915-1920) MARCH, by Author: Oscar Fredrik Strokirk]
2 CONT
2 CONT II. The second branch of the Appelbom family descends from Anders Appelbom, born 1614 and died 1686 and buried 1687. He rests with his first wife, Malin Anderson, in the Appelbom tomb vault in Fellingsbro church. On either side of
2 CONC  the Appelbom family coat of arms in the chancel are their portraits in full size, carefully renovated in 1896 by the artist Jernberg at a cost of 400 kr. These were originally found on Sörbyholm, but were moved after the reign of
2 CONC  Charles XI, when this property, along with many others, passed out of the family, to the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Appelbom wrote to Sörbyholm and Vesslingsbyholm in Fellingsbro, which included the farms Kjänäs, Harparboda, Åby, Hoboda and to Lunda on Lofön, Ullevi in ​​Köping parish and Risinge in Skunkeby parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had inherited in part, even redeemed all of his father's properties in Fellingsbro except Österhammar with Furunäs and Sköldberga, which went to his brother Samuel and he also increased his estates there through new land acquis
2 CONC itions. He thus became the owner of Spannarboda, Mossboda, a farm in Spånga and Blixter-boda. At Sörbyholm he established a bar iron hammer, which was operated until the beginning of the 19th century. In addition, he purchased or 
2 CONC received in grant a great deal of redemption interest from other farms within the parish. According to the land records, he had, during the lands, partly under the protection of 2 hemman in Nybble, all of Fyrby, Vesslingby, Åby, T
2 CONC åje, Oby, Spångboda, Eskarboda, Östra Boda and Villeboda and 1 hemman in each of Lund and Norra Ekeby.
2 CONT
2 CONT As can be seen from this, the county governor, or as he was usually called, the war councilor Appelbom, was a powerful large landowner and a significant person in Fellingsbro. However, it was not long after his death in 1686 befor
2 CONC e all these properties passed out of the family's possession. Some were sold by the death house to the merchant David Feiff, the rest, including all the redemption interest, were affected by Carl XI's reduction.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders son Anders Appelbom inherited Sörbyholm and Vesslingbyholm in Fellingsbro from his father, but he was only allowed to keep them for four years, because in 1690 they were withdrawn to the crown during the reduction of Charle
2 CONC s VI and did not return further in the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT He became a war chamberlain, commissar in the Norwegian army in 1658 and registrar in the chancellery. He is said to have finally become an officer in Holland and died abroad. Married to Anna Behmer, born after 1643, daughter of c
2 CONC ourt councillor Daniel Behmer no. 480 and Brita Schütte. Her portrait is kept in the sacristy of Fellingsbro church and has the note on the back "Married to the minister in Holland Harald Anderson son Appelbom", which is obviously
2 CONC  a confusion between her husband and his uncle the minister in The Hague.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
