2 CONT TAB 1
2 CONT Peder Hansson (översiktstab. 1). Borgare och rådman i Gävle. Död 1612. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift med Ingrid Pedersdotter i hennes 1:a gifte (gift 2:o med rådmannen i Gävle Mårten Hansson Rödbeck), född 1574. Dotter av borgaren och handelsmannen i Gävle Peder Pedersson från Hälsingland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elias Pedersson Gavelius. Född i Gävle. Se Tab. 2
2 CONT Peder Pedersson Gavelius, född 1601. Se Tab
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.bostream.nu/erik.martin.slakt/pdabaafcd.html ]
2 CONT This is where the chaplain Daniel comes into the picture. It is unlikely that Ingelheim would have left it to his son Nils to decide priest's name. Consultation with the clergy in Åsele may have occurred. After Daniel Edin, who di
2 CONC ed in 1708, served John Erik Sjöberg, born 1681, who khde in Åsele during the period from 1712. He may have entered the Daniels place "name giver" for Nils. Why was the "Gavelin" you might wonder. Why not Gafselius or Gavelius exa
2 CONC mple? Maybe you should not underestimate these early Gafsele-bors skills, but it was really the name Gavelius already appeared (dated from Hälsingland stammering shopkeeper and magistrate in Gävle Peder Hansson Helsing, born in 15
2 CONC 00s and died in 1612 in Gavle, His great future family Gavelius named after hometown Gävle). One of the first representatives of the genera were son Elias Pedersson Gavelius, d 1668. He had a total of 24 children (!) (Sv Biogr dic
2 CONC tionary 1964-66, Vol 16, p 761). Elijah's brother Peder Gavelius (1601-45) was the father of Marten Gavelius (d 1709), who with director title managed CG Oxenstiernas goods, among these goods Fullerö in Vasteras Barkarö parish of 
2 CONC Västmanland, Lake Mälaren just south of Västerås. (He could possibly have called themselves Gavelin allegedly by CA "Noppe" Lewenhaupt to Ivar Gavelin in January 1992 ...) (?)
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Gavelin was occupied by Jacob Gavelin in Vasa, who in 1717 held funeral sermon after the late Michael Gavelius: "Then in his life-Postal Inspectors and Rådmannens from Wasa city in Österbotn, Ähreborne and Esteemed Mr. Mi
2 CONC chael Gavelii andelöse flesh Christel again, and with honor Promoted to thes hwilorum on January 13, 1717 Ahr, Blefwo fölliande lines of personal wyrdnad skrefne of Jacob Gavelin. " (The speech starts from 1st Chronicles 29 verse 
2 CONC 15: "Wij are strangers and aliens to you / as were all our fathers"). - Speech is signed "with filial wyrdnad" as if Jacob Gavelin was the son of Michael Gavelius. But he was not! Who was Jacob Gavelin? Well, his name was Jacob Hå
2 CONC kansson, "which in the early 1700s became a priest in Vaasa and called themselves Gavelin" (See Tidskr "Relatives and Featured 'No 2/93 s 390). (It is implicit that his father was Håkan Olofsson, brother of Elsa Olofsdotter, who w
2 CONC as the mother of "Helena sanek / SANIK of Wasa," Helena Johansdotter, who was sister to "curate in Kvevlax" colleague Daniel LinkedIn Åsele. (They fled to Sweden during the "Great ofredens year "in 1710 ta1et and died there.)
2 CONT
2 CONT (Jacob Gavelin married in 1719 with artist Margaret Capsia, which among other things was responsible for the decoration of churches in Ostrobothnia. She was born 1690, d 1759, but lived with her husband Jacob in Vaasa until 1730 w
2 CONC hen they moved to Turku and she becomes an even more prominent artist, now in Finland, and he becomes dean and domkyrkosyssloman därstädes with the new surname Haqvini Gavelin, lazy. kind of Håkansson.)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
