1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Von_G%C3%BCntersberch_nr_685 '''Elisabet von Günthersberch'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift med''' ryttmästaren [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Aminoff_nr_456#TAB_122 '''Johan Fredrik Aminoff'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Correction''' about the parents here and on the page in Swedish.
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is verified information about Elisabet Aminoff’s parents: Gunilla Peräsalo, an amanuensis at the Finnish House of Nobility, refers to the 2008 Supplement to *Elgenstierna; Genealogical Tables of the Swedish Nobility*, p. 419.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabet was ''not'' the daughter of Christoffer v G and Brita Maria Strömberg, BUT rather the daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Joachim-Nicolaus-von-G%C3%BCnterberch/6000000013015733945?through=6000000007707630525 Joachim 
2 CONC Nicolaus v G] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Elisabeth-von-Cronman/6000000007707630525?through=6000000013015733945 Elisabet Cronman]
2 CONT Unfortunately, I cannot copy the information from the Word document I created
2 CONT
2 CONT Furthermore, this information is already included in Carpelan’s Genealogical Tables, as well as in Aminoff-Winberg’s Genealogical Tables, Volume 1 (2017) and Schulman’s family history (Schulman, Hugo: The Schulman–von Schulmann Fa
2 CONC mily in Sweden, Finland, and the Baltic States. Tampere 1938) and Aminoff’s family history (Aminoff, Berndt Herman: The Aminoff Family. Ekenäs 1978)
2 CONT
2 CONT Information on “noble coats of arms…” found online is not an “official” source of facts; it is updated (?) but cannot always be considered accurate, according to amanuensis Gunilla Peräsalo
2 CONT Best regards,
2 CONT Mathias
2 CONT
2 CONT info; House of Nobility Genealogical Tables 2021
